@@ -111,0 +112,13 @@
+
+
+## Secret — Fatal Exception, milestone A
+
+Descriptor: `src/data/secret-cutscene.js`; registry key `secret`, controller kind `system`. `rarities.js` marks Secret's reveal with `cutscene: 'secret'`. A plays fakeout 2400 / black 1600 / boot 6000 ms, then a temporary 600 ms release and existing 400 ms flip (11 seconds total). Safe and Full share these times. Fast uses the existing 70% scale. The completed 40-second descriptor will be assembled in B/C, without adding time to pulls or the three-second charge.
+
+`cutscene-gl.js` extracts compilation, uniforms, render targets, fullscreen vertex and the unchanged crystal bloom/composite shader. `cutscene-screen-engine.js` owns a low-resolution OS upload, ping-pong feedback, tearing, channel shift, pixel-sort approximation, 8x8 quantization, datamosh holds, CRT and noise. Later acts enable its unused corruption controls. Medium disables sort/quantization, Low uses Canvas scanline/CRT fallback, and lost/unavailable WebGL falls back to Canvas. Shader/target warm-up uses the existing dissolving/cutting hook.
+
+`cutscene-safety.js` owns profile selection, the pre-roll and the final output limiter. The actual displayed reveal canvas is sampled after composition, at 64x36, in linear luminance. Large-area opposing changes are tracked against accepted output, in wall-clock time rather than story time, including Fast/scrub changes. Temporal blending is remeasured before acceptance; a prohibited opposing event freezes the previous output. Safe has rate and calm-period gates; Full has a 125 ms minimum alternation interval, 600 ms burst limit, 1500 ms cooldown and 8000 ms total budget. The dev meter uses these measured frames, independent of declared beat events.
+
+`secret-background.js` is shared by the temporary last scene, retained background and finish. Its seed is the reserved serial; the reveal's shared clock feeds the finish while the backdrop is active. Safe inversions are 4.8 seconds apart with 800 ms crossfades and a 0.4 Hz sweep cap; shelf and restrained policies are static. H will add glyph resurrection and the first inversion using this renderer. Skip uses the shared two-second hint and 500 ms black fade; A then enters the temporary release. Recovery follows the existing pending-reveal restore path and restores the deterministic field, without replay. No acquisition state or reward code changes.
+
+A dev-only Play Secret action uses the existing sandbox preview path. Profile, quality, timeline/rate, section jumps and the measured flash meter share the Cutscenes group. The full Short/calm narratives, D–H beat library and Safe caps on older ceremonies are deferred to B/C.
